!=========================================================================!
!                                                                         !
! C1 and C2 chemistry is taken from GRI-MECH version 1.2                  !
!                                                                         !
! Changes made by Vovelle et al, Combust Flame, 2009                                                                 !
!                                                                         !
! (1) C2H + H2 = C2H2 + H  --->   k updated based on new measurments      !
!                                                                         !
! (2) CH2 + O2 = HCO + OH  --->   CH2 + O2 = CO2 + H + H with the same    !
!                                 rate coefficient.                       !
!                                                                         !
!     reason: to boost CO2 and H concentration                            !
!                                                                         !
! (3) C2H3 + O2 = HCO + CH2O ---> rate coefficient of Bozelli-Dean used.  !
!                                                                         !
!     additional reaction channels for C2H3O added.                       !
!                                                                         !
!     reason: to properly account for C2H3 oxidation near main flame zone !
!                                                                         !
!=========================================================================!
